-- title:
--   Node chart of the blown-up Drinfeld curve: completion O[[U,V]]/(UV-π^m)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a complete discrete valuation ring $O$ (a domain, discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal) with $\mathfrak m_O=(\pi)$, together with a nonzero $\varpi\in\mathfrak m_O$ written $\varpi=\pi^m\varepsilon$ with $m\ge 1$ and $\varepsilon\in O^\times$. Let `pr` be a chart presentation for $q,O,\varpi$: power series $f,u,v\in O[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$; put $S=O[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\varpi^{q+1})v-fu)$ with quotient map $\mathrm{mk}_S$. Assume $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0)$ is a non-zerodivisor on $S$, $q\in\mathfrak m_O$, and $a\in O$ satisfies $a^q-a\in\mathfrak m_O$. In $L=S[1/\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0)]$ set $\iota_0:O\to L$ the constants map, $y$ the image of $X_0$, $x=\iota_0(\varpi)/y$, $w=$ (image of $X_1$)$/y$, and $R_0\subseteq L$ the subring generated by the image of $S$ together with $x,w$. The assertion: $\iota_0(O),x,y,w\subseteq R_0$; the ideal $\mathfrak m_a=(\iota_0\pi,y,x,w-\iota_0 a)$ of $R_0$ is maximal; $xy=\iota_0(\varpi)$; $\mathcal N=(R_0)_{\mathfrak m_a}$ is noetherian with maximal ideal $(\iota_0\pi,x,y)$, containing $w-\iota_0 a$, and every element of $\mathcal N$ is congruent modulo that maximal ideal to $\iota_0(o)$ for some $o\in O$; and there is a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal N$ at its maximal ideal onto $O[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-C(\pi^m))$ carrying $\iota_0(o)$ to the class of $C(o)$, carrying $x$ to $U(\pi^m)\gamma$ for some unit $\gamma$, and carrying $y$ to $V(\pi^m)$.
--
--   This identifies the local rings at the $q+1$ ends of the exceptional Drinfeld component, after blowing up the chart and localising at the branch of slope $a$, as ordinary double points of thickness $m$: the completion is the crossing model $O[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^m)$. It is the computational input to [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_X_zero_div_not_mem`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_X_zero_div_not_mem), which transports the conclusion to the blow-up chart itself.
